<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35331" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-paucus</span></b> , a, um, adj.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>very
			little</i>, <i>very few</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">homines,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Eun. 3, 1, 19</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in tmesi: per pol quam paucos reperias
					amatores,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Hec. 1, 1, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">patres,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 43, 11, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">si perpauca mutavisset,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Ac. 2, 43, 132</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dicere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Leg. 1, 12, 34</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perpauca loquens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 1, 4, 18</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gens perpauca,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Ecclus. 48, 17</span></i>
			.—<i>Sup.</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 3, 20,
				5</span></i>.</div>
